# No nested ternaries

A ternary whose branch is another ternary is an error (`oxlint` rule `no-nested-ternary`, SonarQube `typescript:S3358`). Fix it before finishing.

Use `if` / `else if`, or a lookup, and keep each remaining ternary to one decision.

```ts
// Bad
const label = sent ? "Sent" : pending ? "Sending…" : "Resend email"

// Good
let label = "Resend email"
if (sent) label = "Sent"
else if (pending) label = "Sending…"
```

A single ternary is fine: `hidden ? "Show" : "Hide"`.
